{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1057225-questions-on-lairs-and-chambers","id":1057225,"title":"Questions on Lairs and Chambers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-02T13:34:25-08:00","id":1057225,"title":"Questions on Lairs and Chambers","content":"Being part of a dream space, Lairs and Chambers are governed less by feet and inches, and more by a sort of internally consistent logic, yes? That being the case, how does it shake out when a Chamber (a house, for instance) contains areas that, thematically speaking, could be Chambers in their own right (a basement, or an attic)? Are they all part of the same dream space, and as such are all the same Chamber? Or would you need to assign a separate Chamber for each discrete region? And if the latter, what happens if someone in the 'house' tries to go into the basement-that-isn't-there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:45:32-08:00","id":1057263,"title":"","content":"Either is fine. If the Chamber makes sense as a whole spooky house then it's all of it, if instead its more thematic for it to be just one portion of a house (main area, garage, basement, attics, single bathroom, etc) then it is that.<br /> <br /> For the second part, again it depends on the thematics. Doors could open into a void for that extra-dimensional fear, or you could go down the stairs to the basement and find yourself coming down the stairs from the second floor back to where you started. Exits can also serve as Burrows to get to other Chambers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:48:52-08:00","id":1057266,"title":"","content":"IIRC, it could be both. If the seperate rooms were chambers, the doorways etc. would be the burrows connecting them.<br /> If the whole house would be the chamber, then there would be little difference among the different rooms, I think. As in, the attic might be just an open space if its an empty house, or simply filled with stuff if the house is cramped, but you wouldn't have a cramped attic if the rest of the house was empty. If someone enters a basement that isnt there, this could be a possible way to escape the Lair, I guess?<br /> Don't take my word for it, didn't read it in a while.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: what ElvesofZion said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  Boy do I type slowly -.- 03-02-2017, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join 